1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:08,932
Wish and if only behave like a type two or type three if clause: the tense goes one step back to show the thing is not so.

2
00:00:08,932 --> 00:00:11,315
I wish I knew the answer: I don't.

3
00:00:11,315 --> 00:00:13,841
I wish I had listened to you: I didn't.

4
00:00:13,841 --> 00:00:16,536
I wish you would stop shouting: annoyance.

5
00:00:16,536 --> 00:00:18,281
If only I had known earlier.

6
00:00:18,281 --> 00:00:22,591
It is high time we left: something overdue, with the past.

7
00:00:22,591 --> 00:00:24,791
And he talks as if he knew everything.

8
00:00:24,791 --> 00:00:30,664
So never I wish I would have gone, but I wish I had gone; and it is time we went, not go.

